# Options (local additions).
# Format: see data/README.md. Fields:
#   section:                 which part of the program the record configures: logic, derivation, parsing, ...
#   set:                     turns an on/off option on
#   unset:                   an on/off option that is left off
#   option:                  'name:problem-selector', e.g. noErrMess:{"1.7","1.72"}
#   login:                   program login for the course server, 'user:password'
#   font-size:               font size
#   backup-count:            number of server backups to keep
#   backup-name:             name of the server backup set
#   restore-name:            name of the backup set to restore from
#   instance-port:           port used to allow only one running copy
#   option-o:                (not used by the program)
#   disable:                 rules disabled for the selected problems, 'RULES:selector'
#   disable-all-forms:       like disable, applied to every form of compound rules
#   manual:                  rules that must be applied without the program's help
#   manual-all-forms:        like manual, applied to every form of compound rules
#   assume-weakly:           rules/theorems that may be used without proof (weakly assumed)
#   assume:                  rules/theorems that may be used without proof
#   activate-rules:          rules offered for the selected problems
